<h3 id="guide-welcome-to-freedme" tabindex="-1">Welcome to FreeDME</h3>
<p>FreeDME connects neighbors who want to give, lend or receive free mobility equipment. This guide explains how to create an account, offer or request equipment, arrange pickup, complete an exchange and manage your preferences.</p>
<p>A donor offers equipment. A recipient requests it for themselves or as a caregiver. You can use your member account for both activities. Free to keep means a gift; Free Loan means the equipment must be returned by the agreed loan end date.</p>
<h4>Choose your journey</h4>
<p>Donors: register, describe your equipment, submit it for review, respond to requests and arrange pickup. For a loan, confirm the return when it happens.</p>
<p>Recipients: register, find equipment, confirm your document details, request the item and agree on pickup. Confirm receipt and return borrowed equipment on time.</p>
<h4>Before you begin</h4>
<ul>
<li>FreeDME currently serves the nine-county San Francisco Bay Area in California. Registration requires a supported town or ZIP code.</li>
<li>Use your own mobile number. Caregivers should use their own identity and location evidence when requesting equipment.</li>
<li>Keep street addresses and private information out of public listings and equipment photos.</li>
<li>You and the other participant arrange transport and pickup. Meet at a public, nonresidential place in daylight while it is open.</li>
<li>The hosted site sends real SMS. Optional notifications depend on consent and delivery availability; check My Activity for the current transaction state.</li>
</ul>
<p>During prelaunch testing, a separate website password prompt may appear. Use the reviewer credentials supplied by the organizer; this prompt is separate from your personal mobile sign-in.</p>
<h3 id="guide-registration-and-navigation" tabindex="-1">Registration and navigation</h3>
<h4>Create your account</h4>
<ol>
<li>Choose Sign In, then Create an account. You may also be routed to registration when donating or requesting equipment with an unregistered mobile number.</li>
<li>Enter your display name, Location (ZIP code or town) and mobile phone number. Select a matching Bay Area location suggestion; do not enter a street address.</li>
<li>Review the optional SMS consent and the linked Privacy Policy and SMS Terms. Choose whether to receive optional notifications.</li>
<li>Select Verify mobile and register. Enter the verification code sent to your phone and complete verification. Your account is created after mobile verification.</li>
<li>Continue to the donation or request you started. If the equipment is no longer available, choose another listing.</li>
</ol>
<p>If your location is outside the supported area, the form displays: “FreeDME is currently available only for Bay Area, California community members”. Use your actual location; do not select a different town to bypass the restriction.</p>
<h4>Sign in and sign out</h4>
<p>For an existing account, enter your mobile number and select Send verification code. Enter the code sent to your phone. Member sign-in does not require a password. A full US number with +1 is an unambiguous format; use the same number you registered.</p>
<p>Choose Sign Out in the website header when finished, particularly on a shared device. On a small screen, open the menu to find navigation links. Staff sign-in is separate and is not needed by donors or recipients.</p>
<h4>Find your work in My Activity</h4>
<ul>
<li>My Equipment: your own listings, newest first, with status above the equipment title. A recipient with no listings may see an empty tab.</li>
<li>Requests &amp; Handoffs: incoming and outgoing requests. Choose View transaction to respond, arrange pickup or confirm handoff and return.</li>
<li>Questions &amp; Answers: item-specific questions and answers grouped under the equipment title, with an individual status for each question.</li>
<li>SMS Messages: recent messages and delivery status.</li>
</ul>
<p>The selected My Activity tab is remembered. Equipment titles open detailed views; use Back to My Activity when available to return. My Account is a separate top-menu page for personal preferences.</p>
<h4>Verification code problems</h4>
<p>Check the phone number and wait for the code. Follow the page instructions if it expires or fails. Do not repeatedly submit guesses or share a code with another person. If you cannot access the registered number, contact <a href="mailto:inquiry@mobilityexchange.org">inquiry@mobilityexchange.org</a>.</p>
<h3 id="guide-offer-equipment-as-a-donor" tabindex="-1">Offer equipment as a donor</h3>
<h4>Describe and photograph your equipment</h4>
<ol>
<li>Select Donate Equipment. Enter a clear Listing title and choose the Category, including Other when appropriate.</li>
<li>Enter a town or ZIP code in Location. Choose Free to keep for a gift or Free Loan for a loan. For a loan, select a future Loan Until date.</li>
<li>Choose Condition and enter a useful Description, including dimensions, weight, capacity, whether it folds and relevant limitations.</li>
<li>Add 1–5 JPEG or PNG photos of the actual equipment. Each must be at most 5 MB and 25 megapixels. Select them one at a time or together; each selection adds to the collection.</li>
<li>Wait for image screening. Accepted images show a green check and ACCEPTED; rejected images show a red cross and REJECTED. Remove rejected photos and supply suitable replacements before submitting.</li>
<li>Read and truthfully confirm the required disclosures, then select Submit for review. Read the acknowledgement and return to My Activity to see the new listing.</li>
</ol>
<h4>Required disclosures</h4>
<ul>
<li>This equipment is not missing any parts.</li>
<li>This equipment is fully functional.</li>
<li>The above disclosures are truthful to the best of my knowledge.</li>
</ul>
<p>The current form includes Requires Repairs as a condition but still requires the fully functional disclosure. If you cannot truthfully confirm all disclosures, do not check them simply to submit. Ask support for guidance on whether the equipment is eligible.</p>
<h4>Review and publication</h4>
<p>New submissions remain private while PENDING REVIEW. A moderator decides whether to publish or reject them. A publication notice may be sent if notifications are enabled. Automated image acceptance does not guarantee listing approval or certify the equipment’s safety.</p>
<p>Check your listing state in My Activity after submitting.</p>
<h4>Edit or reopen a listing</h4>
<p>In My Equipment, choose Edit Equipment when available. Update the details and photos, then submit for review. Choose Cancel and discard edits to leave without saving. Editing is not offered for reserved, loaned or donated equipment.</p>
<p>For an UNAVAILABLE listing, confirm “I still have this equipment and it is available,” then choose Make available again when appropriate. Do not reopen equipment that you no longer have or that should not be offered.</p>
<h3 id="guide-find-and-request-equipment" tabindex="-1">Find and request equipment</h3>
<h4>Review the listing</h4>
<ol>
<li>Open Find Equipment and select an equipment title. Read the description, condition, location and photos.</li>
<li>Check whether the offer is Free to keep or Free Loan. For a loan, review the Loan Until calendar date and ensure you can return the equipment.</li>
<li>If you need clarification, use Ask A Question. A question does not reserve equipment.</li>
<li>Select Request this Item and sign in if prompted. Complete the identity-document step before sending the request.</li>
</ol>
<h4>Upload and scan your document</h4>
<p>Both gifts and loans currently require evidence of your name and residential address. Choose Utility bill or Government-issued ID. A document without a residential address will not supply all required information; use suitable evidence showing both your name and address.</p>
<ol>
<li>Upload one clear JPEG, PNG or single-page PDF, up to 20 MB. PDFs must be unlocked; multi-page PDFs are not supported. Images must be non-animated and no more than 50 megapixels.</li>
<li>Read and provide the processing consent shown on the form, then submit for scanning. Wait for the progress indicator to finish.</li>
<li>On Confirm your document details, check the first name, last name, residential address and ZIP code against your document. No request has been sent yet.</li>
<li>Correct spelling or name-splitting errors in the first and last name fields. ZIP formatting is normalized automatically. If the address or ZIP information is wrong, upload a clearer or different document rather than confirming incorrect details.</li>
<li>Confirm that the information describes you, and consent to share your name and ZIP code with the named donor for this equipment.</li>
<li>Choose Confirm and submit request. Check Requests &amp; Handoffs for the resulting request.</li>
</ol>
<h4>Caregivers and private information</h4>
<p>If requesting for someone you care for, provide your own evidence, not that person’s. Donors see your name and ZIP code for the request; they do not receive the uploaded document image. Authorized staff may view retained evidence for review.</p>
<p>Scanning extracts text and you confirm the details. A “Verified” label is not independent authentication of the document or person. Corrected names may be identified as requester-corrected in parts of the website.</p>
<h4>If scanning fails</h4>
<p>Use a sharp, well-lit image with the complete name and address visible. Upload a different permitted document if necessary. Do not confirm inaccurate information. Choose Cancel to leave the request flow without submitting it.</p>
<h3 id="guide-review-requests-and-ask-questions" tabindex="-1">Review requests and ask questions</h3>
<h4>Donor response to a pending request</h4>
<ol>
<li>Open My Activity → Requests &amp; Handoffs and choose View transaction.</li>
<li>Review the recipient name and ZIP code, equipment title and response deadline. The pending response window is 48 hours.</li>
<li>To approve, enter a proposed Day and time (Pacific Time) and Public pickup location, then select Approve. Include a specific public venue and meeting point, not just a town.</li>
<li>If you do not wish to accept this request, select Decline. If the equipment is no longer available, select Unavailable.</li>
<li>After approval, watch for the recipient’s acceptance or alternative proposal. Approval alone does not confirm a physical handoff.</li>
</ol>
<p>FreeDME generates notifications for the approval, decline or unavailability as appropriate. Notification delivery depends on consent and service availability. Review the transaction page for the saved outcome.</p>
<h4>Recipient response and expired requests</h4>
<p>The initial donor offer has a 24-hour response window. Open the transaction promptly to accept the suggestion or propose different arrangements. A pending request expires after 48 hours without the required donor response; an unanswered offer also expires after its deadline.</p>
<p>For an EXPIRED request, Requests &amp; Handoffs provides Request Again and Remove Request. Request Again is subject to the listing being available and may require current evidence and consent. A successful retry removes the old duplicate expired listing from your activity. Remove Request removes it from your view; it is not a request to erase all transaction records.</p>
<h4>Ask and answer equipment questions</h4>
<ol>
<li>Recipient: open the equipment details and select Ask A Question. Enter an equipment-related question and submit it. Questions are available for published, available equipment offered by another user.</li>
<li>Donor: open Questions &amp; Answers in My Activity. Find the pending question and select Answer. Enter your reply and choose Submit answer.</li>
<li>Recipient: return to Questions &amp; Answers to read the response. Select Ask Another Question for a follow-up when the listing remains eligible.</li>
</ol>
<p>Questions for the same equipment are grouped under one title. Each has its own status, so a new question does not overwrite an earlier answer. Alerts tell the other participant to check the website; do not include private document details or sensitive information in a question.</p>
<p>Conversations may be marked ARCHIVED after the exchange ends. Archived questions are no longer offered an answer action. Use support for an unresolved issue that cannot be handled through the available controls.</p>
<h3 id="guide-arrange-pickup-and-complete-exchanges" tabindex="-1">Arrange pickup and complete exchanges</h3>
<h4>Agree on the latest pickup proposal</h4>
<ol>
<li>Open View transaction in Requests &amp; Handoffs. Read Suggested handoff, including who proposed it, the Pacific Time date and time, and the location.</li>
<li>If the other participant’s suggestion works, select Accept suggested handoff.</li>
<li>Otherwise, select Suggest a different day/time or location. The current values are prefilled; change what is needed and choose Send suggestion.</li>
<li>The other participant reviews the new suggestion and accepts it or proposes another. Check the newest proposal before making travel plans.</li>
</ol>
<p>RESERVED does not by itself mean the latest pickup details are agreed: a recipient’s counterproposal can also reserve the equipment. Look for HANDOFF ARRANGEMENT ACCEPTED on the current proposal. If the page says the proposal changed, reload it and review the latest details.</p>
<h4>Meet safely</h4>
<ul>
<li>Use a public, nonresidential place in the Bay Area and meet in daylight while the venue is open.</li>
<li>Agree on transport and a clear meeting point. FreeDME does not arrange transport.</li>
<li>Inspect the equipment and confirm that it is suitable before taking it. A listing approval or image check is not a physical safety inspection.</li>
<li>If the meeting does not happen, do not select a confirmation button that says it did. Contact support if you cannot resolve the situation through the transaction controls.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Confirm the actual handoff</h4>
<p>After the equipment is physically transferred, either participant can select Confirm actual handoff on a RESERVED transaction. A gift becomes COMPLETED and the listing becomes donated. A loan becomes LOANED. Do not use this button merely to accept a meeting time.</p>
<p>If a reserved handoff remains unconfirmed, a pickup follow-up may be sent 24 hours after the agreed pickup time. Open the linked website page to update the transaction; the current message does not ask for YES or NO SMS replies. Moderators may also follow up on a reservation that remains unconfirmed for seven days.</p>
<h4>Return a loan</h4>
<p>Return the equipment by the Loan Until date. Once it has actually been returned, either participant can select Confirm equipment returned. The transaction becomes COMPLETED and the listing becomes unavailable until the donor confirms availability again.</p>
<h4>Cancel before handoff</h4>
<p>While the transaction is PENDING, OFFERED or RESERVED, use Cancel request / offer if needed. Recipients may use Revoke consent and cancel before handoff. These controls are unavailable after handoff; privacy requests remain available through My Account.</p>
<h3 id="guide-my-account-and-privacy" tabindex="-1">My Account and privacy</h3>
<h4>Manage SMS preferences</h4>
<ol>
<li>Open My Account from the top menu. Find SMS Preferences and check whether optional notifications are ON or OFF.</li>
<li>Update the optional-notification consent checkbox and select Save SMS preference.</li>
<li>Continue checking My Activity for requests and pickup changes even if you turn notifications off.</li>
</ol>
<p>Sign-in verification codes are separate from optional notification consent. If you previously replied STOP, follow the support instruction on My Account to restore notifications; changing a checkbox may not clear a carrier-level block. Contact <a href="mailto:inquiry@mobilityexchange.org">inquiry@mobilityexchange.org</a> for assistance. The SMS Terms explain STOP, HELP and messaging conditions.</p>
<h4>Change your mobile number</h4>
<ol>
<li>In My Account, select Change mobile number.</li>
<li>Choose Send code to current number, then enter the six-digit code and verify it.</li>
<li>Enter the New mobile number and choose Send code to new number.</li>
<li>Enter the new number’s code and choose Verify and change mobile number.</li>
<li>Review SMS Preferences again. Optional SMS consent does not transfer automatically to the new number.</li>
</ol>
<p>Your current number remains active until both verification steps succeed. Use Cancel to leave the process. If you cannot access your current number, contact support. Do not create a duplicate account simply to bypass recovery.</p>
<h4>Read the policy or request deletion</h4>
<p>Under Privacy &amp; Deletion, choose Privacy Policy to read the current policy or Privacy &amp; Deletion to request removal of your account and personal records. Read the confirmation carefully and submit only when intended. A submitted request awaits administrator review; it does not immediately delete the account.</p>
<p>The deletion process removes your personal data while preserving appropriately reviewed records belonging to the other participant. Shared transaction history may remain under a non-contactable “Deleted account” label. Ask support about your request rather than assuming disappearance from a tab means permanent deletion.</p>
<h4>What happens to request documents</h4>
<p>Source identity-document images are deleted after seven days or at exchange end, whichever comes first. For a gift, retention ends on handoff confirmation or seven days after the latest mutually accepted pickup time, whichever occurs first. For a loan, it ends on return confirmation. A retention timer does not establish that the handoff occurred.</p>
<p>Extracted details and other private operational records follow the longer retention rules in the Privacy Policy and explicit deletion process. Questions and answers are archived at exchange end. Consult the policy for the full scope rather than treating source-image deletion as deletion of every associated record.</p>
<h3 id="guide-status-labels-and-troubleshooting" tabindex="-1">Status labels and troubleshooting</h3>
<h4>Understand the main statuses</h4>
<ul>
<li>PENDING REVIEW: the donor’s listing is waiting for moderator screening. It is not yet publicly available.</li>
<li>AVAILABLE: the listing can receive a request, subject to current availability and eligibility checks.</li>
<li>PENDING: a submitted request awaits the donor’s response.</li>
<li>OFFERED: the donor approved and proposed pickup details; the recipient must respond.</li>
<li>RESERVED: the equipment is held for the exchange. Check whether the newest pickup proposal has also been accepted.</li>
<li>LOANED: handoff of a loan has been confirmed; return is still outstanding.</li>
<li>COMPLETED: a gift handoff or loan return has been confirmed.</li>
<li>EXPIRED: a request or offer passed its response deadline.</li>
<li>UNAVAILABLE: new requests are closed until the donor can appropriately make the listing available again.</li>
</ul>
<h4>Common problems</h4>
<p>Photo rejected: remove it, read the displayed error and add a clear image of the actual equipment. Avoid people and private information. Images not recognized as equipment can be rejected. If all suitable photos fail, contact support.</p>
<p>Form cannot be submitted: complete fields marked with *, check limits and wait for screening to finish. After an error, text may be preserved but newly selected files may need to be selected again. Never make a disclosure you cannot truthfully confirm.</p>
<p>Incorrect document extraction: correct name spelling where permitted. Upload a clearer or different document for incorrect address information. Wait for the scan to complete before trying again.</p>
<p>Missing notification: check your number, SMS preference and whether you previously sent STOP. Review My Activity directly. A saved action and a delivered message are separate events; do not repeat a transaction action just to send another alert.</p>
<p>Equipment or proposal changed: reload the page and inspect the latest state. Availability can change while you are completing a form. Do not assume an old page still permits the same action.</p>
<p>A button is missing: available actions depend on the transaction state and your role. For example, cancellation is unavailable after handoff and editing is unavailable while equipment is reserved or loaned.</p>
<h4>Get help</h4>
<p>Use Resources &amp; help for How It Works, frequently asked questions, mission and team information. For account, privacy or unresolved service questions, contact <a href="mailto:inquiry@mobilityexchange.org">inquiry@mobilityexchange.org</a>. Include the equipment title, approximate time and a brief description. Never send passwords, verification codes or identity-document images in ordinary support messages.</p>
<p>This guide follows the current member screens and later owner decisions. It is a companion to the Moderator and Administrator Operator Manuals. The live Privacy Policy and SMS Terms provide the detailed policy wording.</p>
